codex
The failure is caused by the audit sandbox’s PID namespace: Lean asks `/proc/<namespace-pid>/exe`, while the mounted `/proc` exposes a different PID namespace. I’m applying a narrowly scoped local runtime shim that rewrites only `/proc/<digits>/exe` reads to `/proc/self/exe`; this restores executable discovery without changing Lean code, project sources, or theorem checking. I’ll record the shim source and use it consistently for every Lean/Lake command.
